Ladybird formats console text from bounded previews of stored values.
It never calls accessors or proxy traps for those previews. DOM text
summaries read element names and IDs directly, and connected DevTools
keeps expandable object references with bounded preview contents.

This follows the distinction the other engines make between previews
and explicit inspection. Blink uses V8ConsoleMessage::wrapArguments
and ObjectMirror previews; ValueMirror::getProperties represents script
accessors without calling them, while allowing selected native getters.
WebKit bounds previews in RemoteObject._generatePreview, and handles
accessors in RemoteObject._appendPropertyPreview. Gecko uses its
WebConsoleActor.createValueGrip method and the DOMNode previewer for
node metadata, with separate actors handling subsequent inspection.

The console text limits and representation are Ladybird-specific.
The live object protocol and its retention policy remain intact.
